Advertise the OAuth discovery metadata ChatGPT needs to pick a public-client grant, taken from
home-assistant/core.

Without "token_endpoint_auth_methods_supported", a client has to assume the RFC 8414 default
("client_secret_basic") and sends its token request as a confidential client - which Home Assistant
answers with 400 "Invalid client id", so the connector fails after a successful login. ChatGPT's own
client metadata declares "token_endpoint_auth_method": "private_key_jwt" with ["none",
"private_key_jwt"]; the announcement below is what makes it choose the public-client path. The same
commit allows CORS on both discovery documents.

Upstream commit, re-anchored onto this release (same changes, tests omitted):
  ef31c2d9ca  Correct OAuth discovery metadata for public clients (#184254)

Delete together with the PKCE backport in this directory once nixpkgs ships Home Assistant 2026.10.x.

diff --git a/homeassistant/components/auth/login_flow.py b/homeassistant/components/auth/login_flow.py
--- a/homeassistant/components/auth/login_flow.py
+++ b/homeassistant/components/auth/login_flow.py
@@ -122,6 +122,7 @@
     """View to host the OAuth2 information."""
 
     requires_auth = False
+    cors_allowed = True
     url = "/.well-known/oauth-authorization-server"
     name = "well-known/oauth-authorization-server"
 
@@ -139,6 +140,9 @@
             "authorization_endpoint": f"{url_prefix}/auth/authorize",
             "token_endpoint": f"{url_prefix}/auth/token",
             "revocation_endpoint": f"{url_prefix}/auth/revoke",
+            "grant_types_supported": ["authorization_code", "refresh_token"],
+            "token_endpoint_auth_methods_supported": ["none"],
+            "revocation_endpoint_auth_methods_supported": ["none"],
             # Home Assistant accepts URL-based client_ids via IndieAuth without
             # prior registration, and discovers allowed redirect URIs from link
             # tags or a Client ID Metadata Document served at the client_id URL.
@@ -163,6 +167,7 @@
     """View to host the OAuth2 Protected Resource Metadata per RFC9728."""
 
     requires_auth = False
+    cors_allowed = True
     url = "/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource"
     name = "well-known/oauth-protected-resource"
 
